2.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Dolby Laboratories, Inc. engages in the design and manufacture of audio, imaging, accessibility, and other hardware and software solutions for television, broadcast, and live entertainment industries in the United States and internationally. The company develops and licenses its audio technologies, such as AAC, HE-AAC, and extended HE-AAC, a digital audio codec solution; AVC, a digital video codec used in STBs, mobile devices, cameras, and broadcast television services and other products; and Dolby Atmos and Dolby Vision include encoding technologies that artists use to create more compelling and immersive audio and video experiences. It also provides DD+, an advanced surround sound audio codec technology; Dolby AC-4, an audio codec that uses cutting edge compression; and HEVC, a digital video codec that compresses video. In addition, the company offers Dolby Cinemas, a premium large format cinemas that deliver a Dolby branded premium cinema offering with Dolby Vision, Dolby Atmos, and a Dolby theater design; Dolby.io, a SaaS product of immersive, interactive, and social experiences with real-time engagement for live events, especially sports; and digital cinema servers, cinema processors, amplifiers, loudspeakers, and audio and imaging hardware and software products for the cinema, television, broadcast, communication, and entertainment industries. Further, it provides various services to support theatrical and television production for cinema exhibition, broadcast, and home entertainment. It serves film studios, content creators, post-production facilities, and broadcasters. Dolby Laboratories, Inc. was founded in 1965 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Marc  Whitten | President, CEO & Director | Age 54","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $710K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $180K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $67K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Dolby Laboratories is a mid-cap industrials business with a $5.4B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 9% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it. Gross margins of 89% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $360M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 25 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.55\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.6pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $2.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Gross margin tops the Industrials peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Among the least levered in Industrials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Dolby (DLB) Stock Fair Value Moves Lower As Analysts Cut Growth Views","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/dolby-dlb-stock-fair-value-130837240.html","date":"2026-11-21","timestamp":1795266517.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.963,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(DLB) Risk Channels and Responsive Allocation","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/35/DLB_Risk_Channels_and_Responsive_Allocation_112026055602_1795215362.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795215362.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is 